     Rules of the game:     Players take turns placing game pieces on the board.     Pieces must be placed so that they "surround" a line     of the opponents pieces, with one of your pieces on     each end.  On each turn, pieces owned by the opponent     which are surrounded by the newly played piece and a     piece already on the board are flipped, and become     owned by the current player.  When all 64 squares have     been filled or there are no possible moves for either     player, the game ends and whoever has the most disks     wins.  A disk must be played on every turn when possible.